      "html": "<img class=\"source-facsimile\" src=\"assets/arp-apq-m2-011-appendix-1.png\" alt=\"Appendix\n\nDetails of outstanding matters relating to impairment\n\nDunk operates across several different divisions. Although none of the divisions have previously been\nimpaired, evidence now suggests that the assets of three of these divisions (Divisions E, F and G) may\nbe impaired and an impairment review is to be undertaken. Divisions E, F and G are considered cash-\ngenerating units.\n\nInformation in relation to the property, plant and equipment (PPE) and the intangible assets of these\ndivisions are as follows:\n\n                                          E        F      G       Total\n                     Assets                      £’000      £’000      £’000      £’000\nCarrying amount      PPE                        304       389       178       871\n                          Intangible assets               90                -                -        90\n                                                394       389       178       961\n\nFair value                Division assets                400       440       180      1,020\n\n                     Year ended\nValue in use                                      354       390       148\n\n    •  The intangible asset in Division E relates to a patent which has an estimated fair value less\n        costs of disposal of £88,000. It has not been possible to estimate the value in use for the\n        patent.\n    •  None of the other individual non-current assets generate cash flows independently from the\n         rest of the non-current assets in the division.\n    •   In addition to the carrying amount of non-current assets allocated to each division, there is\n        goodwill of £85,000 which cannot be split between the three divisions. It is estimated that the\n       combined recoverable amount of each cash generating unit is £980,000.\n    •   Costs of disposal are estimated to be 10% of fair value for each division.\n    •  Any impairment loss is considered to be material and must be presented separately.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                                               13\">"
